  "aiMeta": {
    "narrative": "The rule receives a booking context (cabin code, fare brand, and Executive Club loyalty tier). It seeds a working object with all output fields, copies the request fields onto it, then performs two reference lookups: the cabin code is resolved to a cabin group (First / Business / Premium / Economy) via ref-cabin-classes, and the loyalty tier is resolved to a numeric rank via ref-loyalty-tiers. From the cabin group it computes the base free checked-bag allowance (First=3, Business=2, Premium Economy=2, Economy=1, but Basic economy=0). It then computes a loyalty bonus (Gold +2, Silver/Bronze +1, Blue +0) and sums these into the total checked-bag allowance. Finally it sets the per-bag weight limit (32kg for premium cabins, 23kg otherwise) and returns the full allowance. Hand baggage is a fixed 2 pieces (one handbag/laptop bag plus one cabin bag) per the BA hand-baggage policy.",
    "nodeExplanations": {
      "n2": "Creates the starter working object containing every field the response will carry, with safe defaults.",
      "n3": "Copies the inbound cabinCode, fareType, and loyaltyTier from the request onto the working object.",
      "n4": "Looks up the booked cabin code in the Cabin classes table and stores its cabin grouping (First/Business/Premium/Economy) as cabinClass.",
      "n5": "Looks up the Executive Club loyalty tier in the Loyalty tiers table to obtain its numeric rank used for bonus baggage.",
      "n6": "Derives the base free checked-bag allowance from the cabin group, with Basic economy fares granted no free checked bag.",
      "n7": "Calculates extra checked bags earned by loyalty status (Gold +2, Silver/Bronze +1, Blue none).",
      "n8": "Adds the base cabin allowance and the loyalty bonus to produce the total checked bags allowed.",
      "n9": "Sets the per-bag checked weight limit (32kg in premium cabins, 23kg otherwise) which finalises the eligibility result."
    },
